@@ -189,6 +189,26 @@ For compatibility, gorget still accepts `vendor` entries under `fetch:` and
 moves them before the declared transform steps. This syntax is deprecated;
 new and updated pipelines should declare vendoring under `transform:`.

+A pin's `version` accepts a string or, for Yarn, an array of versions.
+A string sets a package-wide minimum. An array sets minimums within matching major versions.
+Array pins preserve other major versions and versions above each minimum.
+Gorget reads the lockfile and generates the required resolutions.
+Dependency names in array pins can use glob patterns.
+Gorget also retargets existing Yarn `patch:` references and retains their patch files.
+The package manager must still apply each patch successfully.
+The source transaction publishes the manifest and lockfile only after all updates succeed.
+
+```yaml
+transform:
+  - type: vendor-bump
+    ecosystem: yarn
+    pins:
+      - dependency: axios
+        version: "1.20.0"
+      - dependency: brace-expansion
+        version: ["1.1.18", "2.1.4", "5.0.9"]
+```
+
 Transforms use a Git checkout when one is active. Otherwise, they extract the
 sole fetched source archive. A `vendor` step can select an archive by its output
 name through `source`, including when fetch also downloads signatures or keys:
